Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Customs Post at Valença
- Story & Context: Recorded inside an abandoned border guard shack between Portugal and Spain where the Barani-Medrano wedding procession was temporarily detained for lacking transport carnets, this track captures the exact moment the ceremony turned into an impromptu, all-night sit-in. Bandleader João propped his massive baritone saxophone on the customs counter, blasting low-end ostinatos through a battery-powered amplifier while Kadiatou rallied both feuding circus factions with blistering, unquantized rap bars over an unyielding 118-BPM motorik groove. By the time the smell of burnt clutch fluid and spilled guava nectar filled the damp border office, even the carabineros were clapping out polyrhythms, transfixed as Kadiatou declared over the speaker horn: "We tore down the fence to weave a brighter tightrope." The track serves as the mythical genesis of the genre, immortalizing the night a legal checkpoint became a dance floor.
